 with safe zones. Subscription  | $99/yr Premium  | $44.99/yr web (or $4.99/mo) · $7.99/mo + $44.99/yr App Store\nWhat it unlocks  | Two-way Google & Outlook sync, chores with tickets & rewards, the meal grid, Family Inbox & Magic Import, kiosk mode, open API  | Calendar sync, meal planner, budget tracker, shared documents, recipe box, location sharing\nYear one, family of four  | $99  | $44.99\nEvery year after  | $99  | $44.99\nThree years  | $297  | $134.97\n\nFamilyWall prices from familywall.com's Premium page, support.familywall.com's Premium article and the App Store listing, checked 18 September 2026. Paying monthly instead of annually costs more over three years: $179.64 on the web, $287.64 through the App Store.\n\nSources: familywall.com: Premium, support.familywall.com: what's included in Premium, FamilyWall App Store listing\n\n### What you get back\n\n  * Your calendar, synced both ways with Google and Outlook by default, without needing a paid tier\n  5. Set up kiosk mode on a spare tablet if a Home Hub was the plan.\n\n## Frequently asked\n\nCan I export my data from FamilyWall?+\n\nFamilyWall doesn't publish a data-export tool for calendar events, chores or documents, so the practical move is reconnecting the calendar account you already sync (Google, Outlook or an ICS feed) rather than exporting from FamilyWall itself. Anything typed only into FamilyWall, a chore checklist, a budget note, a shared document, needs to be photographed or forwarded into Plannie's Magic Import by hand.\n\nDo I need to cancel my FamilyWall Premium subscription?+\n\nYes, separately. Signing up for Plannie doesn't touch a FamilyWall subscription; cancel it through whichever store you subscribed from, familywall.com's account settings or the App Store's subscriptions page, so you're not paying for both.\n\nWhat happens to my FamilyWall messages and documents?+\n\nThey stay in FamilyWall unless you copy them out yourself. Plannie has no messenger or document storage, so save anything you need, a shared file, a chat thread, before you stop paying for Premium and lose access to it.\n\nDo I need to buy anything to switch?+\n\nNo. Plannie's kiosk mode runs on any tablet your family already owns, so there's nothing to buy to replace FamilyWall's waitlist-only Home Hub. Plannie has a free plan too, so you can try the move before paying for Premium.\n\nWhat does Plannie cost compared to FamilyWall?+\n\nPlannie Premium is $99 a year for the whole household, $297 over three years. FamilyWall Premium is $44.99 a year (or $4.99 a month) on the web, $134.97 over three years, but $7.99 a month and $44.99 a year through the App Store. Plannie's single price includes calendar sync, chores, meals, the assistant and kiosk mode; several of those need FamilyWall's paid tier, and others, a messenger, a budget tracker, location sharing, aren't things Plannie does at all.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n‎FamilyWall: Family Organizer App - App Store (https://apps.apple.com/ca/app/familywall-family-organizer/id496889629?platform=vision)\nciteturn92search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; \n\n    * Identifiers\n    * Usage Data\n    * Diagnostics\n\nPrivacy practices may vary, for example, based on the features you use or your age. Learn More\n\n## Information\n\nSeller\n    \n\n  * Family & Co\n\nSize\n    \n\n  * 199.8 MB\n\nCategory\n    \n\n  * Productivity\n\nCompatibility\n    Requires iOS 17.0 or later.\n\n  * iPhone\nRequires iOS 17.0 or later.\n  *   * iPad\nRequires iPadOS 17.0 or later.\n  *   * Apple Vision\nRequires visionOS 1.0 or later.\n\nLocation\n    \n\n  * This app may use your location even when it isn’t open, which can decrease device battery life.\n\nLanguages\n    English and 10 more\n\n  * English, Dutch, French, German, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, Russian, Spanish, Swedish\n\nIn-App Purchases\n    Yes\n\n  * Monthly FamilyWall Premium $6.99\n\n  *